								Ranger Bait<br />
								Moderator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14489<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13971#msg13971"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13971#msg13971">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> January 27, 2005, 10:24:21 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13964#msg13964">Quote from: Garadan on January 27, 2005, 08:34:19 am</a></div><div class="quote">With my my semi departure from the game the guild kinda lost direction, motivation... not sure which or what. But as we all know or should know RL &gt; EQ. Ascent really only had a handful of old school ascent left in the guild. A few of us either decided to quit the game as well or transfer. The game really lost its fun factor to be honest from my point of view. Once Kinladar lost his cool and went down, shit just got blah.  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /><br /></div><br />Nah, I just saw that there was so little skill left on the server capable of getting to the highest end, and most of that already spoken for, and more leaving the game on a daily basis, that I saw no sense in attempting a full rebuilding, even if that was what FoT needed from the ground up from the begining.<br /><br />The merged guild concept was a bad one from the begining, the thing we worked out with RoS for a bit was just going to be an alliance, but some people got upset that we&#039;d be taking a couple steps backward as we helped RoS gear up, and move through some content.<br /><br />Either way, it came down to a majority of the guild mad about alot of the drama caused by certain people, (those people went to Ascent btw, not every FoT who went to ascent caused drama, but the 2-3 in mind did) and I should have listened to the officers, and kicked them a long time ago, but in general I thought it would work out, and I saw so little skill up and coming in the raiding ranks of guilds lower than us compared to what we had, that I was at that time willing to tolerate alot.<br /><br />Such is life. <br /><br />The guild we have created in WoW on Medivh is a simple affair, mostly old Anthology people, with a few real life friends tossed in, and a couple new people we&#039;ve met on Medivh joining. But we&#039;ll never fall into the trap of massive recruitments, and that bullshit, either they are well known by the guild and accepted, or they don&#039;t get to stay. No compromises like we sometimes allowed for on skills in EQ.<br /><br />Only annoying thing is, few alliance people pickin Mages or Priests to play&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/banghead2.gif" alt="banghead2" border="0" /> 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13972"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
