								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13972#msg13972"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13972#msg13972">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> January 27, 2005, 10:49:34 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Just dropping in to salute one of the great guilds in EQ.&nbsp; Always sad when a guild breaks up, especially one as old and acclaimed as Ascent.&nbsp; I hope that those who are now guildless find new guild homes where they&#039;re happy.&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
